  "issue": {
    "headline": "Every vote, tied to the money that preceded it",
    "body": "Dallas publishes its agendas, minutes and roll-call votes through Legistar as structured data — which means the record of who voted for what is machine-readable, and can be lined up against the contract awards and zoning cases on the same agenda. Very little of that comparison has ever been done in public.",
